   566	/// Note that printable text is delivered via `print_slice` actions
   567	/// (runs of codepoints) whenever the stream can decode multiple
   568	/// codepoints at once, and via `print` actions otherwise. Handlers
   569	/// that care about text must handle both.
   570	///
   571	/// A handler may also have a `vtPrintAscii` function, which receives
   572	/// instead of `print_slice` the runs the stream already knows are
   573	/// printable ASCII (0x20 to 0x7F), as the input bytes, so neither side
   574	/// widens or classifies them:
   575	///
   576	///   fn(bytes: []const u8) void
   577	///
